e-awareness-training walkthrough log — 2026-10-10
Worked-case lesson: no command line by design (brief §6).
The "run" is the one-year program plan authored and self-reviewed in-session
against NIST SP 800-50 Rev. 1 (PDF fetched 2026-10-10, 2,178,096 bytes,
87 pages; csrc landing confirms: published September 2024, supersedes SP
800-50 (2003) and SP 800-16 (1998)).

Key verified fact driving the lesson: Rev. 1 deliberately retired the
awareness/training/education three-tier split — research with federal training
managers showed the terms meant different things to different people and caused
confusion; the replacement is CPLP (Cybersecurity and Privacy Learning
Program), applied generically, goal = learning opportunities at every career
stage. Verified in the PDF text in-session.

Scope: fictional Copperline Freight (240 staff, 3 sites). Plan: needs
assessment (3 observed failures: dispatcher credential phishing, finance wire
fraud pattern, driver personal-device messaging); 5 audience segments with
behavioral objectives; quarterly topic calendar; monthly phishing simulations
with ramping difficulty; simulation rules of engagement written before first
run (learning not punishment, no shaming, no HR pipeline, report-rate as
headline metric, executives included); metrics split effectiveness (report
rate, time-to-report, behavior recurrence) vs activity (completion);
ownership (awareness lead to CISO, CEO sponsor) + quarterly risk-committee
reporting.

Unverified lead (logged, not cited): SANS Security Awareness Planning Kit page
(sans.org) fetched 2026-10-10 but JS-rendered with no extractable text
(109,134 bytes raw, ~0 chars readable) — excluded from §7 per the
no-verification-URL-no-row rule; CISA awareness materials used instead.

